  "gradeRuleDescribe": {
    "yms_year": 114.0,
    "yms_smester": 2.0,
    "cls_id": "CE08310",
    "sub_id": "78101",
    "scr_dup": "001",
    "tpa_score_new": "<div>The learning outcomes of lecture are evaluated by:</div>\n\n<div>1. Two paper examinations</div>\n\n<div>2. One oral presentation</div>\n\n<div>3. Participation&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>The following items are required for lab practice.</div>\n\n<div>1. Approved safety goggles for everyone</div>\n\n<div>2. Lab coat for everyone</div>\n\n<div>3. Lab manual for each group</div>\n",
    "tpa_score_new_en": null,
    "course_pol": "For the Lab session (on Fridays), we will lecture in the classroom 工108 from 2:10 to 2:40 (approximately). We will then enter the Lab (工202) after the lecture. When you enter the lab, you have to wear a lab coat and safety goggles. No shorts or skirts are allowed in the lab. During lab practice, you can't wear contact lenses. You can't bring food or drinks into the lab, either.\nFor Lecture session (on Tuesdays and Fridays), keeping your attention is the most important issue.",
    "course_pol_en": "Course Policies\n1.Attendance is very very important.\n2.It would be not allowed to pass two oral presentations, or you will fail in this course.\n3.This is an EMI course.\n4.Please use English as much as possible.\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1.出席率很重要\n2.兩次口頭報告一定要參加\n3.這是一個EMI課程別忘記\n4.請盡量使用英文",
    "course_rem": null,
    "course_rem_en": null,
    "ais_meno": "<div>Copy&nbsp;of the lab report sheet or pre-lab report is not allowed. No cheating on pre-Lab Exam and Practical Exam (final).&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>Copy&nbsp;of the lab report sheet or pre-lab report is not allowed. No cheating on pre-Lab Exam and Practical Exam (final).&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>Copy&nbsp;of the lab report sheet or pre-lab report is not allowed. No cheating on pre-Lab Exam and Practical Exam (final).&nbsp;</div>\n",
    "ais_meno_en": "<div>Students are expected to adhere to the highest standards of academic integrity. This includes honesty in all academic work, proper attribution of sources, and avoidance of any form of academic dishonesty such as plagiarism, cheating, or fabrication. Violations of academic integrity may result in severe consequences, up to and including failing the course.</div>\n",
    "ilearn_mk": "N"
  },
